181 0 obj
<<
/Author (Hunter Hughes)
/CreationDate (D\07220261106060018\05505\04700\047)
/Creator (H Heuristics)
/Keywords (polycrisis resilience\054 Development Capability Index\054 economic convergence\054 Global South\054 technological diffusion\054 clean transition\054 climate adaptation\054 vulnerability reduction\054 deficit stacking\054 human development\054 disaster mortality\054 systemic risk)
/ModDate (D\07220261106060018\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (This report sets out the H Heuristics Polycrisis Resilience Framework\054 a development\055oriented framework developed by Hunter Hughes\054 Founder of H Heuristics\054 for reducing vulnerability to multiple interacting and compounding crises\056 It defines Polycrisis Resilience as the capacity of individuals\054 communities\054 societies\054 economies\054 institutions and interconnected systems to withstand\054 adapt to\054 recover from and reduce vulnerability to interconnected risks\056 Its central proposition is that improving the underlying economic\054 technological\054 environmental and institutional conditions of societies can progressively reduce their vulnerability to compounding global risks\054 so that development is treated not only as a route to higher incomes but as a fundamental mechanism of resilience\056 It is the third report in the Polycrisis Resilience series\054 after the founding report and a report on the clean transition\056)
/Title (Polycrisis Resilience\072 The H Heuristics Framework\072 How Economic Convergence\054 Technological Diffusion\054 Clean Transition\054 Adaptation and Human Development Can Reduce Vulnerability to Interconnected Global Crises)
/Trapped /False
>>
endobj
